    "title": "Hebron Residents: 2026 Supplemental Motor Vehicle and Real Estate Taxes Due January 1 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 hours ago The Town of Hebron's Revenue Collection Department announced that Supplemental Motor Vehicle taxes and the second installment of Real Estate taxes for 2026 are due starting January 1, 2026. Payments can be made at the Tax Collector’s office in Hebron Town Hall at 15 Gilead St during business hours.\nPayments must be received or postmarked by February 2, 2026, to avoid interest charges. Taxes not paid by this date will be charged interest at 1.5% per month from January 1, 2026. The minimum interest charge is $2.00 per installment.\nActing Tax Collector Brigit Tanganelli issued this notice on December 3, 2025. Residents are reminded that not receiving a bill does not remove their responsibility to pay.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
